# Example 12: a morph movie with captions and pauses at key frames.
# HNH nuclease domain docking in SpCas9, between two observed states:
# the checkpoint state 7Z4L, where HNH is ordered but undocked, and the
# catalytic state 7Z4J, where it is docked on the scissile phosphate.
# Pacesa et al. 2022, Nature 609:191.
#
# A morph is an interpolation, not data. It shows how two endpoints
# differ; it does not show a pathway, and the intermediate frames are not
# observed structures. Say so on the movie, as the caption here does.
#
# Choosing the endpoints is the whole job. A morph silently drops every
# residue not modelled in both inputs, so if the domain you want to
# animate is disordered in one endpoint it vanishes from the movie and
# you animate nothing. Check before rendering:
#     morph #1,2 frames 2 modelId #9
#     info residues #9/B
# and confirm the residue range you care about is in the list. The
# Taylor-lab multi-turnover series looks like the obvious source here and
# is the wrong choice: HNH is unmodelled in one of those states, so
# residues 764 to 924 are absent from that morph entirely.
#
# Rules for a movie:
#   hold on each endpoint long enough to read the caption, about 1 s
#   caption every held frame, so a viewer joining mid-loop knows the state
#   one continuous camera; do not rotate and morph at the same time
#   pin the morph model id, never guess it from the open order
open 7z4l
open 7z4j
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc

# Protein chain only. Chain B is the protein in both entries, not A.
delete #1/A,C,D
delete #2/A,C,c,D

# corkscrew keeps a rotating domain from sweeping through the body of the
# protein the way a straight-line interpolation can.
morph #1,2 frames 90 method corkscrew cartesian false modelId #9

open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc
hide #1,2 models
color #9 lab_gray_p
color #9/B:775-908 lab_hnh
color #9/B:906-918 lab_vermillion
cartoon style #9 xsection oval width 1.4 thickness 0.4

view #9
turn y 30
view #9 pad 0.06
windowsize 1000 750

2dlabels text "SpCas9  HNH docking" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.95 size 22 color lab_black bold true
2dlabels text "HNH" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.83 size 18 color lab_hnh bold true
2dlabels text "L2 linker" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.79 size 18 color lab_vermillion bold true
2dlabels text "interpolation between two observed states, not a measured pathway" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.02 size 14 color lab_gray
2dlabels create caption text "checkpoint  7Z4L" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.89 size 20 color lab_state1 bold true

movie record supersample 3 size 1000,750

# Hold on the checkpoint state
coordset #9 1,1 ; wait 30

# Checkpoint to catalytic
2dlabels change caption text "docking" color lab_gray
coordset #9 1,90 ; wait 90

# Hold on the catalytic state
2dlabels change caption text "catalytic  7Z4J" color lab_state4
coordset #9 90,90 ; wait 40

movie encode hnh_morph.mp4 format h264 quality high framerate 30
